      "content": "thanks for the code. i'm worried that manually adding wrappers to every single call might be too much overhead or might miss something if a library is doing its own allocations. is there a way to implement a \"canary\" or some kind of pattern to detect when memory is being \"stolen\" or lost silently without having to wrap everything? maybe some kind of integrity check on the heap?",
